Deferred features {#deferred}
=============================

*This section is non-normative.*

<table class="data">
  <caption>Features deliberately out of scope for v0.1.0</caption>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Feature<th>Deferred to<th>Reason
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>Streaming and wrapped streaming methods
      <td>v0.2
      <td>SSE, interruption, and chunk-level policy are too much surface.
    <tr>
      <td>Batching atomicity, ordering, cross-request dependencies
      <td>v0.2
      <td>Standard JSON-RPC 2.0 batching is permitted in v0.1; ACS-specific atomicity,
          ordering, and dependency rules wait for the streaming spec.
    <tr>
      <td>Sensitivity and four-level timeout model
      <td>v0.2
      <td>Categorization-from-facts is non-trivial; v0.1 uses a single
          handshake-negotiated default timeout.
    <tr>
      <td>Recursive ASK and quorum
      <td>v0.2
      <td>Bounded delegation and tie-breaking need careful specification.
    <tr>
      <td>Multi-tenant isolation rules
      <td>v0.2
      <td>Touches policy, SessionContext, audit, and A2A.
    <tr>
      <td>`protocols/A2A/*` wrapping specification
      <td>v0.2
      <td>A2A hook wrapping is reserved — the namespace exists — but the detailed method
          mapping waits ([[#binding-a2a]]).
    <tr>
      <td>AgBOM federation across A2A peers
      <td>v0.2
      <td>Single-agent AgBOM is in v0.1; federated views need an A2A-side discovery method
          first.
    <tr>
      <td>gRPC and unix_socket transports
      <td>v0.2+
      <td>HTTP and stdio cover IDE, SaaS, and on-premises in v0.1.
    <tr>
      <td>PQC as RECOMMENDED default
      <td>Future
      <td>Promote `ML-DSA-65` once ecosystem readiness justifies it.
    <tr>
      <td>Classical-only signature deprecation
      <td>Future
      <td>Deprecate classical algorithms once PQC-only is universal.
</table>

Roadmap {#roadmap}
==================

*This section is non-normative.*

<table class="data">
  <caption>Version roadmap</caption>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Version<th>Theme<th>Highlights
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>**v0.1.0**
      <td>Baseline and profiles
      <td>ACS-Core (mandatory), ACS-Trace, ACS-Inspect / ACS-Inspect-Dynamic,
          ACS-Provenance, ACS-Crypto, and ACS-Audit profiles.
    <tr>
      <td>**v0.2.0**
      <td>Async and composition
      <td>Streaming, wrapped streaming, batching atomicity / ordering / dependency
          semantics, recursive ASK, quorum, multi-tenant isolation, a policy-author
          attestation profile, the Cedar binding, connection reuse, a sensitivity-tier
          timeout model, and AgBOM federation across A2A peers.
    <tr>
      <td>**v0.3.0+**
      <td>Reach and transport
      <td>gRPC and unix_socket transports, A2A and MCP `deny` / `modify` extensions,
          classical-only signature deprecation, and the full deployment-mode taxonomy.
</table>

